            <ArticleTitle>Pain syndromes in the setting of haematopoietic stem cell transplantation for haematological malignancies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>757-64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/bmt.2008.3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe pain syndromes may be recorded during all phases of haematopoietic stem cell transplantation (HSCT) for haematological malignancies: from stem cell mobilization to the long-term post transplant period. Although the major cause of pain in the setting of HSCT is injury to mucosal tissues induced by the conditioning regimen, pain from several other causes has been reported. In this paper, we review pain and its management in the setting of HSCT.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
